{"subject":"RHET","courses":[{"code":"RHET 101","subject":"RHET","number":"101","level":100,"title":"Principles of Writing","credits":4,"creditsMax":4,"description":"[IAI Code: C1900] Instruction in structuring academic, argumentative essays, including how to develop thesis statements and use evidence across different types of writing. This course is the first semester of a two-semester sequence ( RHET 101 - RHET 102 ) that fulfills the campus Composition I general education requirement. This course includes weekly individual tutorials. Credit is not given toward graduation for: Credit is not given for both RHET 101 and RHET 105.","prereqCodes":["RHET 101"],"prereqText":"Placement in RHET 101.","prereqNote":"","genEd":["Composition I"],"sameAs":[],"noise":false,"url":"https://catalog.illinois.edu/courses-of-instruction/rhet/"},{"code":"RHET 102","subject":"RHET","number":"102","level":100,"title":"Principles of Research","credits":4,"creditsMax":4,"description":"[IAI Code: C1901R] Continued instruction in structuring academic, argumentative essays; concentrating on the use of primary and secondary sources as evidence in research-based arguments. Second semester of a two-semester sequence ( RHET 101 - RHET 102 ) that fulfills the campus Composition I general education requirement. This course includes weekly individual tutorials. Credit is not given toward graduation for: Credit is not given for both RHET 102 and RHET 105.","prereqCodes":["RHET 101"],"prereqText":"RHET 101.","prereqNote":"","genEd":["Composition I"],"sameAs":[],"noise":false,"url":"https://catalog.illinois.edu/courses-of-instruction/rhet/"},{"code":"RHET 105","subject":"RHET","number":"105","level":100,"title":"Writing and Research","credits":4,"creditsMax":4,"description":"[IAI Code: C1901R] Introduction in research-based writing and the construction of academic, argumentative essays that use primary and secondary sources as evidence. This course fulfills the Campus Composition I general education requirement. Credit is not given toward graduation for: Credit is not given for both RHET 105 and any of these other Comp I courses: RHET 101, RHET 102, CMN 111 or CMN 112.","prereqCodes":[],"prereqText":"","prereqNote":"","genEd":["Composition I"],"sameAs":[],"noise":false,"url":"https://catalog.illinois.edu/courses-of-instruction/rhet/"},{"code":"RHET 199","subject":"RHET","number":"199","level":100,"title":"Undergraduate Open Seminar","credits":1,"creditsMax":5,"description":"May be repeated.","prereqCodes":[],"prereqText":"","prereqNote":"","genEd":[],"sameAs":[],"noise":false,"url":"https://catalog.illinois.edu/courses-of-instruction/rhet/"},{"code":"RHET 233","subject":"RHET","number":"233","level":200,"title":"Advanced Rhetoric and Composition","credits":3,"creditsMax":3,"description":"Research and analyze audience, purpose, cultural context, and conventions of different writing situations and use that knowledge to compose projects in different genres and modalities. Particular sections will contain a theme, such as writing in the disciplines, the rhetoric of podcasts, or the use of generative AI. Coursework includes invention, drafting, and revision activities throughout the course in a collaborative learning environment.","prereqCodes":[],"prereqText":"Completion of campus Composition I general education requirement.","prereqNote":"","genEd":["Advanced Composition"],"sameAs":[],"noise":false,"url":"https://catalog.illinois.edu/courses-of-instruction/rhet/"}],"sections":[{"code":"RHET 101","subject":"RHET","number":"101","sections":[{"crn":"72174","type":"Laboratory Lecture-Discussion","section":"C C","start":"ARRANGED","end":null,"days":"n.a.","room":null,"building":null,"meetings":[{"days":"n.a.","start":"ARRANGED","end":null,"room":null,"building":null},{"days":"MWF","start":"10:00AM","end":"10:50AM","room":"44","building":"English Building"}],"instructors":["Gaffney, K Gaffney, K"],"partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"08/24/26-12/09/26","availability":"Closed"},